<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andreas Hofer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1767–1810</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andreas Hofer was a Tyrolean innkeeper who led the uprising of 1809 against Bavarian and French rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a>. His peasant militia won several battles at Bergisel near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/innsbruck">Innsbruck</a>, and he governed Tyrol for some months, but after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> made peace the revolt collapsed. Betrayed and captured, he was shot by the French at Mantua in 1810 and became a Tyrolean national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andreas-hofer.jpg" alt="Andreas Hofer" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Wachter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andreas_Hofer_(Wachter).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
